                                                                                <due></due>
                            <votes>0</votes>
                                    <watches>3</watches>
                                                                            <comments>
                            <comment id="494879" author="JIRAUSER19234" created="Thu, 21 May 2026 22:27:09 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://jira.whamcloud.com/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?name=behlendorf&quot; class=&quot;user-hover&quot; rel=&quot;behlendorf&quot;&gt;behlendorf&lt;/a&gt; I was told you may be able to assist with this.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="494881" author="behlendorf" created="Fri, 22 May 2026 00:54:06 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;A quick thing to try is setting the zfs module option `zfs_dmu_offset_next_sync` to `1`.&#160; As long as Lustre isn&apos;t repeatedly dirtying the dnode from another thread holes should be reported reliably.&#160; Quickly reporting holes when a dnode is dirty hasn&apos;t been implemented, but it would be nice!&#160; One other thing to keep in mind is holes will reported at a recordsize granularity (not 4K).&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="495244" author="behlendorf" created="Fri, 29 May 2026 16:50:36 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;OpenZFS issue for this problem: &lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/openzfs/zfs/issues/18402&quot; class=&quot;external-link&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot;&gt;https://github.com/openzfs/zfs/issues/18402&lt;/a&gt;&#160;&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
